# sh-to-py C4b: implement step-2 dispatch

Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).

**Goal**: Port /implement Step 2 implementation dispatch: implementer selection, codex/cursor implement launchers, recovery paths, commit-on-behalf.

**Absorbs (approx lines)**: skills/implement/scripts/step2-implement.sh (1200; 3 .md refs), run-step2-dispatch.sh (103), compute-step2-recovery-paths.sh (121), commit-implementation.sh (70); scripts/launch-codex-implement.sh (448), launch-cursor-implement.sh (376), lib-implement-round-cap.sh (61).

**Notes**: codex/cursor implementer manifest contracts (larch:codex-implementer / larch:cursor-implementer agent prompts) unchanged; launchers build on the B4 framework; agent prompt files re-generated via B6 generators. Harnesses test-step2-dispatch.sh (2123), test-codex-implementer.sh, test-cursor-implementer.sh port to pytest here.

**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: C4a, B4, B6.

**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage; absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.

</feature_description>


